Z||000008||turbo86se||10-25-2001||11:32 AM||||I've been to IRM several times. It's been about four years, but I always called ahead to make sure Barbara was going to be there. Barbara is a very nice lady, very helpful, and didn't mind me walking around the shop checking out all the kit cars and engines.<P>The MillerWoods turbo system on my '86SE was bought and installed at IRM. Barbara still remembers my Fiero. The only turbo-charged black auto '86SE in Maryland! ||||reg||1
Z||000009||WhiteFieroBlur||10-29-2001||11:51 AM||||ok I called these people but she was out, but before I call back and find out about the intergrated rocker panels are these things worth it? I mean $550 dollars come on thats alot. And the guy told me they are backed up on fiberglass orders. For $550 bucks does it come with perfect fitting cause it had better. Well for those of you that has ordered them let me know if the money and wait is worth it.<P> Also I seen many pics like the blue chop top with em on but with a pic its hard to tell. Does it really look good in person on a car?<P> ok and one more thing has anyone orderd them thru these people. The price is like 300 something and seem to be almost like IRM. <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierofiber/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fierofiber/</A> <P> Thanx - Eric||||reg||1
Z||000010||TRiAD||10-29-2001||11:54 AM||||There's aren't nearly as DEEP as IRMs. <P>Makes a big difference...||||reg||1
Z||000011||turbo86se||10-29-2001||02:25 PM||||I saw a set of these on a pink '85GT in MD a few years ago. I don't know how they fit, but they looked awesome. It's up to you, both sets look great. <P>Last year I was put on a waiting list for IRM's 3" wing stands. Took about 2 months or so to get them, but they're awesome. ||||reg||1
